{"id":"gibb-river-road","title":"Gibb River Road","who":"Classic route · the Kimberley by 4x4","when":"Dry season only, about May–October","vehicle":"4x4, 7–14 days, bush camping","kind":"4x4","color":"#b45309","summary":"About 660 km of mostly dirt road across the Kimberley in Western Australia, an old cattle route between Derby and Kununurra: red gorges with swimming holes, river crossings like the Pentecost, cattle stations with campgrounds, and very few people. Carry fuel, water and two spare tyres.","sources":[{"label":"Andy & Ness: the Gibb River Road, part III (September 2025)","url":"https://andyandnessas-allaussieadventures.blogspot.com/2025/09/the-gibb-river-road-part-iii.html"},{"label":"Australia.com: Gibb River Road itinerary","url":"https://australia.com/en/trips-and-itineraries/broome-and-surrounds/the-gibb-river-road-itinerary.html"}],"approximate":"The usual west-to-east stops; the line follows the road where the router found it.","km":1079,"bbox":[122.2237,-17.9562,128.7391,-15.7235],"stops":[{"name":"Broome","place":"Broome, Western Australia","at":[-17.9567,122.224],"text":"Camels on Cable Beach and a last big shop before the Kimberley.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Broome%2C_Western_Australia_11.jpg/500px-Broome%2C_Western_Australia_11.jpg","page":"Broome, Western Australia","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Broome%2C_Western_Australia_11.jpg","credit":"Kat Clay from Sydney, Australia","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Derby","place":"Derby, Western Australia","at":[-17.3032,123.6287],"text":"The western start of the Gibb, with its giant boab trees.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/BoabPrisonTree.jpg/500px-BoabPrisonTree.jpg","page":"Derby, Western Australia","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BoabPrisonTree.jpg","credit":"Martin Kraft","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Windjana Gorge","place":"Windjana Gorge","at":[-17.4071,124.9479],"text":"Freshwater crocodiles sunning under limestone walls of an ancient reef. Nearby, wade through Tunnel Creek.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Windjana_gorge_02.jpg/500px-Windjana_gorge_02.jpg","page":"Windjana Gorge National Park","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Windjana_gorge_02.jpg","credit":"Peter C. Espenschied (Pc-espe at de.wikipedia)","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Bell Gorge","place":"Bell Gorge","at":[-16.9941,125.2042],"text":"Into the King Leopold Ranges: a waterfall into a deep swimming hole.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Margaret_River_in_Flood.jpg/500px-Margaret_River_in_Flood.jpg","page":"Wunaamin Miliwundi Ranges","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Margaret_River_in_Flood.jpg","credit":"Philiphist","license":"CC BY 3.0"}},{"name":"Manning Gorge","place":"Mount Barnett Roadhouse","at":[-16.7166,125.9274],"text":"Swim across the river to walk to Manning Gorge's falls."},{"name":"Ellenbrae Station","place":"Ellenbrae Station","at":[-15.9572,127.0624],"text":"A remote station famous for its fresh scones.","source":{"label":"Andy & Ness (2025)","url":"https://andyandnessas-allaussieadventures.blogspot.com/2025/09/the-gibb-river-road-part-iii.html"}},{"name":"Pentecost River","place":"Home Valley Station","at":[-15.7235,127.8321],"text":"The famous crossing of the Pentecost under the Cockburn Range. Saltwater crocodiles here: drive, don't wade.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Pentecost_River.jpg/500px-Pentecost_River.jpg","page":"Pentecost River","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pentecost_River.jpg","credit":"Bäras","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"El Questro","place":"El Questro","at":[-16.0077,127.9812],"text":"Gorges, Zebedee hot springs and Emma Gorge, worth days, not hours.","source":{"label":"Andy & Ness: El Questro (2025)","url":"https://andyandnessas-allaussieadventures.blogspot.com/2025/09/the-gibb-river-road-part-iii.html"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/El_Questro_Gorge_Waterfall.jpg/500px-El_Questro_Gorge_Waterfall.jpg","page":"El Questro Wilderness Park","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_Questro_Gorge_Waterfall.jpg","credit":"Neil","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Kununurra","place":"Kununurra, Western Australia","at":[-15.7731,128.7388],"text":"Tarmac again, and Lake Argyle nearby."}],"legs":[{"by":"ride","km":224,"line":[[-17.956,122.2237],[-17.9562,122.2411],[-17.93,122.2397],[-17.8891,122.2665],[-17.8437,122.5287],[-17.8235,122.5629],[-17.8198,122.7382],[-17.7558,122.9262],[-17.6407,123.1666],[-17.6679,123.289],[-17.6685,123.4475],[-17.699,123.5232],[-17.7434,123.5821],[-17.7381,123.6429],[-17.6358,123.7382],[-17.5427,123.7434],[-17.4885,123.7296],[-17.4514,123.7459],[-17.3669,123.6744],[-17.3098,123.6485],[-17.3028,123.629]]},{"by":"ride","km":148,"line":[[-17.3028,123.629],[-17.3098,123.6485],[-17.3441,123.6646],[-17.4033,124.0425],[-17.4612,124.2611],[-17.4378,124.3491],[-17.435,124.6813],[-17.3955,124.7544],[-17.4239,124.8556],[-17.412,124.9432]]},{"by":"ride","km":145,"line":[[-17.412,124.9432],[-17.4239,124.8556],[-17.3955,124.7544],[-17.3147,124.8436],[-17.2409,124.8778],[-17.2081,124.9173],[-17.1824,124.9166],[-17.1637,124.9452],[-17.1467,124.9785],[-17.1475,125.0692],[-17.117,125.11],[-17.1071,125.1856],[-17.1427,125.2328],[-17.1245,125.2453],[-17.1328,125.2647],[-17.1753,125.2937],[-17.1632,125.3127],[-17.1706,125.358],[-17.1505,125.3857],[-17.0782,125.2964],[-17.0658,125.2482],[-17.0401,125.2279],[-17.0186,125.2307],[-16.9996,125.207]]},{"by":"ride","km":115,"line":[[-16.9996,125.207],[-17.0186,125.2307],[-17.0401,125.2279],[-17.0658,125.2482],[-17.0782,125.2964],[-17.1505,125.3857],[-17.1474,125.4994],[-17.0621,125.583],[-17.018,125.653],[-16.9633,125.6607],[-16.925,125.6868],[-16.9033,125.7782],[-16.8666,125.8269],[-16.8307,125.8